lowers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FeymoodDEV/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FeymoodDEV/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FeymoodDEV/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FeymoodDEV/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FeymoodDEV/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FeymoodDEV/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FeymoodDEV/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FeymoodDEV/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-23T16:19:40Z","updated_at":"2025-09-23T16:19:40Z","body":"> Does this happen in 4.4.1?\n\nAFAIK, there is no scenario where this could happen in 4.4.1 as abstract methods aren't implemented. You cannot get a method from the parent class through autocomplete (unless it's a builtin virtual).\n\n```gdscript\nextends Node\nclass_name ParentClass\n\nfunc foo():\n\tpass\n# This is a comment\n```\n\n```gdscript\nextends ParentClass\n\n# If I try adding foo through autocomplete, it does not appear as it would in 4.5 with an abstract method.\n```\n\nI can confirm this happens to me as well on the following system config, latest Arch extra repo package for 4.5-1:\n\n* Godot v4.5.stable unknown - EndeavourOS #1 SMP PREEMPT_DYNAMIC Mon, 08 Sep 2025 05:47:21 +0000 on Wayland - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Mobile) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3060 Laptop GPU - AMD Ryzen 7 5800H with Radeon Graphics (16 threads) - 15.02 Gio memory","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3324713712/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":4,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3397505